{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2068 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c4f6b732b713636e7acd1090fa89249af049245b0a011b26df5a0d5300c26c4b" :edb/db-before-t 2067 :edb/db-after-t 2068 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535380 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:06:52.937Z" 13194139535380 true] [17592186179606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346727 13194139535380 true] [17592186179606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346730 13194139535380 true] [17592186179606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346737 13194139535380 true] [17592186179607 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346720 13194139535380 true] [17592186179607 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346724 13194139535380 true] [17592186346720 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346721 13194139535380 true] [17592186346720 1089 "q-353254" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346720 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535380 true] [17592186346720 1100 "The growth rate of the number of students enrolled in an after-school program, $P(t),$ is jointly proportional to the number of students enrolled at time $t,$ measured in weeks, and the difference between the program’s maximum enrollment and the number of students enrolled.\n\nGiven that the constant of proportionality is $0.004$ and the maximum enrollment is $500,$ find an expression for the number of students enrolled after $t$ weeks, given that there were $50$ students enrolled initially.\n\n| $P(t)\\,=\\,\\,$ | $500$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1\\,+\\,$ {{field-1}} |  |" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346720 1113 #uuid "d66b0ab0-fd3c-5d87-be7a-bba9eaae950e" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346720 1145 "Since the number of students enrolled grows at a rate that is *jointly* proportional to the number of students enrolled at time $t$ and the difference between the maximum enrollment and the number of students enrolled, the number of students enrolled follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.004,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=500.$ Therefore, the growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.004\\,P(500-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-(500\\cdot 0.004)t}}=\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-2t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=50$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-2\\cdot 0}} & =50 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{500}{50} \\\\ C & =10-1 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{500}{1+9{e}^{-2t}}.\n$$" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346722 13194139535380 true] [17592186346721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346723 13194139535380 true] [17592186346721 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535380 true] [17592186346721 1041 "field-1" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346721 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346722 13194139535380 true] [17592186346721 1110 #uuid "08604c8c-e1b9-5dee-be5e-c072ca94672c" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346722 1034 "9e^{-2t}" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346722 1111 #uuid "11ec8548-8156-5825-8a3e-8c991cce418a" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346723 1034 "9e^{-t}" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346723 1111 #uuid "bdd18404-6e17-5912-a001-3bf1565a0fc5" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346724 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346725 13194139535380 true] [17592186346724 1089 "q-353256" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346724 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535380 true] [17592186346724 1100 "The growth rate of the number of trees in a reforestation area, $P(t),$ is jointly proportional to the number of trees at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the area’s carrying capacity and the number of trees.\n\nGiven that the constant of proportionality is $\\frac{1}{3000}$ and the carrying capacity is $1500,$ find an expression for the number of trees after $t$ years, given that there were $300$ trees in the area initially.\n\n| $P(t)\\,=\\,\\,$ | $1500$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1\\,+\\,$ {{field-1}} |  |" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346724 1113 #uuid "e8c3a91a-4c08-55c3-b41e-b5dc4f85c448" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346724 1145 "Since the number of trees grows at a rate that is *jointly* proportional to the number of trees at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the number of trees, the number of trees follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=\\frac{1}{3000},$ and the carrying capacity is $a=1500.$ Therefore, the growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=\\frac{1}{3000}\\,P(1500-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{1500}{1+C{e}^{-(1500\\cdot \\frac{1}{3000})t}}=\\frac{1500}{1+C{e}^{-t/2}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=300$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1500}{1+C{e}^{-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0}} & =300 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{1500}{300} \\\\ C & =5-1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{1500}{1+4{e}^{-t/2}}.\n$$" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346726 13194139535380 true] [17592186346725 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535380 true] [17592186346725 1041 "field-1" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346725 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346726 13194139535380 true] [17592186346725 1110 #uuid "6465b12f-27af-5135-ad39-5600febb0324" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346726 1034 "4e^{-0.5t}" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346726 1111 #uuid "e6224e90-b97d-554c-be3c-039a3fd82461" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346727 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346728 13194139535380 true] [17592186346727 1089 "q-353261" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346727 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535380 true] [17592186346727 1100 "The population $P(t)$ of customers signed up for a grocery store’s rewards program follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.35P-0.0007{P}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in months. If there were $120$ customers signed up initially, how many customers were signed up after $7$ months? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nAfter $7$ months, approximately\n{{field-1}} customers were signed up." 13194139535380 true] [17592186346727 1113 #uuid "915582a3-47ae-5196-8aa7-f705f9ce8511" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346727 1145 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.35P-0.0007{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.0007P(500-P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.0007,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=500.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-(500\\cdot 0.0007)t}}=\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-0.35t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=120$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-0.35(0)}} & =120 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{500}{120} \\\\ C & =\\frac{25}{6}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{500}{1+\\frac{19}{6}{e}^{-0.35t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=7$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(7) & =\\frac{500}{1+\\frac{19}{6}{e}^{-0.35(7)}} \\\\  & ≈393.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $7$ months, approximately $393$ customers were signed up." 13194139535380 true] [17592186346728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346729 13194139535380 true] [17592186346728 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535380 true] [17592186346728 1041 "field-1" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346728 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346729 13194139535380 true] [17592186346728 1110 #uuid "a5cd81a5-e2b6-5443-805a-490c398e977d" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346729 1034 "393" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346729 1111 #uuid "c250200d-0f64-5c10-8ac4-ec5064456705" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346730 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346731 13194139535380 true] [17592186346730 1089 "q-83890" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346730 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535380 true] [17592186346730 1100 "The population $P(t)$ of owls in a particular forest follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.1P-0.000\\,2{P}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. If there were $100$ owls in the forest initially, how many owls inhabited the forest after $10$ years? Round you answer to the nearest integer." 13194139535380 true] [17592186346730 1113 #uuid "a08d81ba-fc21-563c-8e11-eb7caf22c807" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346730 1145 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.1P-0.000\\,2{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,2P(500-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,2,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=500.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-(500\\cdot 0.000\\,2)t}}=\\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-0.1t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=100$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =100 \\\\ \\frac{500}{1+C{e}^{-0.1(0)}} & =100 \\\\ 1+C & =5 \\\\ C & =4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{500}{1+4{e}^{-0.1t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=10$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10) & =\\frac{500}{1+4{e}^{-0.1(10)}} \\\\  & ≈202.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $10$ years, approximately $202$ owls inhabited the forest." 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346732 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346733 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346734 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346735 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346736 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1041 "selection" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346734 13194139535380 true] [17592186346731 1110 #uuid "4713e061-bb57-5559-ae21-1781cf141215" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346732 1034 "173" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346732 1111 #uuid "9220e045-52cf-5927-a49d-5ebe280e1360" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346733 1034 "289" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346733 1111 #uuid "cb25506c-8b6d-5ad9-a5e8-2ea6dfe0790e" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346734 1034 "202" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346734 1111 #uuid "5f910854-9f4d-5a10-b8a9-39c1f06ed416" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346735 1034 "214" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346735 1111 #uuid "2ebbcf69-2f81-5012-9af1-3e98cee4ccca" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346736 1034 "366" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346736 1111 #uuid "424ea656-d9e8-5449-a6f1-0f761d89587e" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346737 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346738 13194139535380 true] [17592186346737 1089 "q-83892" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346737 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535380 true] [17592186346737 1100 "The rate of growth in the number of students $P(t)$ in a school who have heard a certain rumor follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=P-0.000\\,5{P}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in hours, since the rumor started spreading. If there were $2$ students who knew the rumor initially, how many students have heard the rumor after $7$ hours?" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346737 1113 #uuid "79a1ac0d-15f0-5ffb-9bf7-5b5bee38a3f8" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346737 1145 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =P-0.000\\,5{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,5P(2\\,000-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=2\\,000.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(2\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,5)t}}=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=2$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =2 \\\\ \\frac{2\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(0)}} & =2 \\\\ 1+C & =1\\,000 \\\\ C & =999\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+999{e}^{-t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=7$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{2\\,000}{1+999{e}^{-7}} \\\\  & ≈1047.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $7$ hours, approximately $1047$ students have heard the rumor." 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346739 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346740 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346741 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346742 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346743 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1041 "selection" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346740 13194139535380 true] [17592186346738 1110 #uuid "f0d863bd-c2d3-51b8-a0da-1526bed583ee" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346739 1034 "1258" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346739 1111 #uuid "b84e1eea-da11-5045-bde6-b82632d50a41" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346740 1034 "1047" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346740 1111 #uuid "94b10ab0-b17d-5e58-a44c-79b2608abd63" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346741 1034 "997" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346741 1111 #uuid "7b5a396a-9db4-5b09-b754-9297d38c2599" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346742 1034 "1521" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346742 1111 #uuid "cb40ca50-f770-584c-b0d8-7c52f3730a98" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346743 1034 "764" 13194139535380 true] [17592186346743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535380 true] [17592186346743 1111 #uuid "9fc57e84-25b2-5ee5-afe7-84ac847340f1" 13194139535380 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-353254" 17592186346720 "q-353254/field-1" 17592186346721 "q-353254/field-1/0a7584ce423f3dd0a9808fa0dd0c7cf53053fd5a6c514ac2ed1704b14fe1f98a" 17592186346722 "q-353254/field-1/7efc7904ce2c8a4cda64cd9bf14f272fd9b7c9e8f7170b35315bc5